+Source vs destination. The adoption flow separates two things that used to be one:
+
+- **target_url** — the site being crawled for reference
+- **destination_domain** — the site being built
+
+`ensure_site_record` creates the record for `destination_domain`. `firecrawl_crawl` hits `target_url`. `apply_adoption_plan` writes provenance (`identity.adopted_from`, `site_specs.notes`, per-page `contentData.adopted_from`, and the `needs_composition` / `needs_design` work item specs) with the source host extracted from `target_url`, while the site row, pages, and work items belong to the destination. The source host is also what keys the crawl-content lookup table inside `apply_adoption_plan` — mismatching source and destination there would silently drop all adopted page content.
+
+If only `url` / `domain` are supplied, source and destination are the same and behaviour matches the original single-domain adoption.
+
+After completion, the dispatch loop picks up work items (`needs_design`, `needs_content_page × N`, `needs_rerender`) on the destination site and builds the site through the normal pipeline.
 
