 ### Adoption modes
 
-| Mode | Trigger | What happens |
-|------|---------|-------------|
-| Take over domain | `./trigger-adopt-site.sh mortgagecalculator.co.uk` | Adoption agent: crawl → classify → recreate → improve |
-| Build inspired by | `{"domain": "loancalculator.co.uk", "reference_sites": ["https://mortgagecalculator.co.uk"]}` | Classifier uses reference in research, strategist takes what's useful, content is fresh |
-| Normal build | `{"domain": "newsite.co.uk"}` | Classifier researches the vertical, finds competitors organically |
+| Mode | Input_data | What happens |
+|------|-----------|--------------|
+| Mirror existing domain (source = destination) | `{"url": "https://site.co.uk", "domain": "site.co.uk"}` or equivalently `{"target_url": "https://site.co.uk", "destination_domain": "site.co.uk"}` | Adoption crawls the URL and builds a site record on the same domain. Legacy single-domain flow. |
+| Separated source/destination | `{"target_url": "https://source-site.uk", "destination_domain": "my-new-site.co.uk"}` | Adoption crawls `target_url` for reference, writes the destination site record as `destination_domain`. `adopted_from` provenance records the source host; pages, work items and specs belong to the destination. |
+| Build inspired by | `{"domain": "loancalculator.co.uk", "reference_sites": ["https://mortgagecalculator.co.uk"]}` | Not the adoption agent — goes through the classifier/planner pipeline. Classifier uses reference in research, strategist takes what's useful, content is fresh. |
+| Normal build | `{"domain": "newsite.co.uk"}` | Not the adoption agent — classifier researches the vertical, finds competitors organically. |
 
